## Viewing History

View commit history:

```bash
git log
git log --oneline            # Condensed view
git log --graph              # Graph view
git log --all --graph --oneline  # Complete overview
```

View specific file history:

```bash
git log <file-name>
```

Show a specific commit:

```bash
git show <commit-hash>
```

---

## Undoing Changes

Discard changes in working directory:

```bash
git checkout -- <file-name>
git restore <file-name>      # Newer syntax
```

Unstage files:

```bash
git reset HEAD <file-name>
git restore --staged <file-name>  # Newer syntax
```

Revert a commit (creates new commit):

```bash
git revert <commit-hash>
```

Reset to a previous commit:

```bash
git reset --soft <commit-hash>   # Keep changes staged
git reset --mixed <commit-hash>  # Keep changes unstaged (default)
git reset --hard <commit-hash>   # Discard all changes
```

---

## Stashing

Save current changes temporarily:

```bash
git stash
git stash save "Description"
```

List stashes:

```bash
git stash list
```

Apply stashed changes:

```bash
git stash apply              # Apply latest stash
git stash apply stash@{n}    # Apply specific stash
```

Apply and remove stash:

```bash
git stash pop
```

Delete a stash:

```bash
git stash drop stash@{n}
git stash clear              # Delete all stashes
```

